\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S14}{\ignorespaces Full factor versus direct surface after ten trading days, with numerical diagnostics, by evaluation seed. Each row uses 1{,}000 paths, and monetary values are in dollars per share. Mean $|\Delta P|$, mean $\Delta $P\&L, and its paired standard error compare the full factor with the direct surface. Outside is the percentage of path dates before expiration on which strike/spot lay outside the 0.8 to 1.2 range of the calibration data. Floor is the largest percentage of simulated dates, across the five IV variants, on which the factor sat at the variance floor. Tree change is the largest absolute price change from 201 to 401 tree steps, across the five variants, on the first twenty paths after ten and twenty trading days.}}{31}{table.caption.30}\protected@file@percent }
